  <reporting-org ref="NL-KVK-27378529" secondary-reporter="0" type="10">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Netherlands Enterprise Agency</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Adding value to Vietnamese Pomelo: Creating superior export quality and innovative fresh-cut</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Partners will establish the first professionally managed fruit chain for pomelos in Vietnam including a state-of-the-art fruit warehousing model and farmer contract system. The project is situated in the Mekong Delta, southern Vietnam. The business concept benefits from the ability of Vietnam to produce the pomelos year-round and so a unique window of opportunity for pomelo exports exists in the period from February until the end of August when the largest exporter (China) has much less pomelos available and prices increase with about 40%.An innovative fruit farmer extension and contract system will be set up which will train pomelo farmers to grow pomelos in a sustainable manner (and of better quality) and which shall offer them a contract that guarantees the sales to the joint venture of their total harvest at a fair price.In the warehouse pomelos will be classified (4 grades) and the best fruit (grade 1 and 2) will be exported. Fruit which does not meet the export quality requirements shall be processed into fresh-cut fruit (the pomelo cleaned, peeled and divided in pieces) or will be sold on the local fruit markets.Some of the employment impact in figures:&#x2022;	At the end of the project (December 2012) 100 direct permanent jobs in the fruit warehouse and in the pomelo sourcing system will have been created and additionally 50 seasonal jobs.&#x2022;	Long-term contracts will be made with 100 pomelo farmers and short term supply contracts with 150 pomelo farmers by 2012.&#x2022;	100 pomelo contract farmers will be trained in GlobalGAP, of which 75 pomelo contract farmers will be GlobalGAP certified by the end of 2012.</narrative>
  </description>
